            <ArticleTitle>Pituitary apoplexy as a first manifestation of pituitary adenomas following intensive thrombolytic and antithrombotic therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>110-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Apoplexy of a previously asymptomatic pituitary macroadenoma may occur in the setting of intensive thrombolytic, antithrombotic, or anticoagulant therapy for acute myocardial infarction. Classic clinical findings may initially be nonspecific and a high index of suspicion is therefore required for early diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
